       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (about 850 mg per dose). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nThe 1700 mg may be a typo or a total daily dose. These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg/day split into two doses**, which is 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose**, if you were thinking of a different regimen.\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose."
      }
